{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when all the men of war… and YHWH spoke to me, etc.</b> But from the sending of the spies until here, nothing is said in this pericah except 'וַיֹּאמֶר' — to teach you that all thirty-eight years that Israel was rebuked, the dibbur did not address him in the language of affection, face to face and with settled mind — to teach you that the Shekhinah does not rest upon the prophets except for the sake of Israel (Mekhilta, Exodus 12)." "<b>The men of war.</b> From twenty years old and upward, who go out in the army."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:41.288658995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}